title: Combining vocabularies
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A tiddler can activate multiple vocabularies at once. List them comma-separated in the type field:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Markdown,Color-Boxes
```

All markers from all listed vocabs become available in that tiddler.

!! Default is the implicit fallback

A plain `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` tiddler (no `;vocab=` parameter) activates `vocab/default` automatically. When you DO list vocabs, Default is no longer implicit. Add it explicitly if you want its markers (`»` paragraph, `.` glyph, `°` degree, ...) alongside the others:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Markdown
```

Vs. just `;vocab=Markdown`, which deactivates Default's markers for that tiddler. [[Example - Markdown]] does the latter to keep the markdown demo focused.

!! Collision resolution

When two vocabularies ship a marker with the same `open` literal, the LAST one in the type field wins. `;vocab=A,B` lets B's marker take over the shared `open`; `;vocab=B,A` lets A's win.

This is also how [[Vocabulary - Fountain]] documents itself: it recommends activating WITHOUT Default so its `.` scene-marker can fire (otherwise Default's `.` DOT marker would intercept).

